      "visualQA": {
        "result": "PASS",
        "notes": "Three marine iguanas counted. Main animal has coherent head, dorsal ridge, visible limbs and one tapering tail; no apparent fused bodies or added limbs. Lava roughness, skin scales and water look photographic. Island/bay composition synthesized and not geolocated; small or occluded toes are not anatomical research evidence.",
